From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 15:58:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: orangepi-5b: disable eMMC CQE

Hot-plugging the USB-C DisplayPort sink can coincide with eMMC command
queue recovery failures on the Orange Pi 5B.  Once CQHCI fails to halt,
the root filesystem loses I/O and its ext4 journal is aborted, leaving the
board wedged until a cold reset.

Keep HS400 enhanced strobe enabled, but disable command queueing on this
board.  This reduces peak eMMC performance in exchange for avoiding the
CQHCI failure path and protecting the root filesystem during display
hot-plug events.

Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5b.dts | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5b.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5b.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5b.dts
@@ -43,6 +43,7 @@
 };
 
 &sdhci {
+	/delete-property/ supports-cqe;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
